    "body": "### Summary\r\n\r\n`TraceLens_compare_perf_reports_pytorch --sheets all` fails with `ValueError: kernel_summary sheet not found` on every report generated without `--enable_kernel_summary` — which is the default for PyTorch reports. The `kernel_summary` sheet is rocprof-specific and requires an opt-in flag at report-generation time, but the comparison tool treated it as mandatory whenever `all` was requested.\r\n\r\n### Implementation\r\n\r\n**`TraceLens/Reporting/compare_perf_reports_pytorch.py`**\r\n\r\nRestructured the `kernel_summary` block in `generate_compare_perf_reports_pytorch()`. If `kernel_summary` exists in the report, process it normally. If it's absent and the user explicitly requested `--sheets kernel_summary`, raise an error explaining that `--enable_kernel_summary` is needed at generation time. If it's absent and the user just said `--sheets all`, skip `kernel_summary`.\r\n\r\n**`tests/test_compare_perf_reports.py`**\r\n\r\nAdded two unit tests:\r\n- `test_sheets_all_skips_missing_kernel_summary` — verifies `--sheets all` succeeds and produces `gpu_timeline` + `ops_summary` results without `kernel_summary` when the sheet is absent.\r\n- `test_sheets_kernel_summary_explicit_raises_when_absent` — verifies that explicitly requesting `--sheets kernel_summary` when `kernel_summary` raises a `ValueError` with a message pointing to `--enable_kernel_summary`.\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\n- Both new tests pass locally.\r\n\r\nCloses #1015",
